# Patternmode Project Guidelines

_The best of the React ecosystem, unified under Base UI primitives with professional Tremor styling._

## Styling Conventions

### Use Object-Based Conditional Classes

When applying conditional styles with `clsx`, prefer object-based syntax over arrays or ternary operators for better readability and maintainability.

**✅ Good - Object-based approach:**

```tsx
className={clsx(
  // Base styles
  "w-full flex items-center gap-3 rounded-md text-left text-sm transition-all duration-200",
  // Layout
  {
    "px-2 py-2 justify-center": isCollapsed,
    "px-3 py-2 justify-start": !isCollapsed,
  },
  // Colors
  {
    "text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300": !current,
    "text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100": current,
  },
  // Background
  {
    "bg-zinc-100 dark:bg-zinc-800": current,
    "bg-zinc-50 dark:bg-zinc-850": isNavigating,
  },
  // Interactive states
  "hover:bg-zinc-100 dark:hover:bg-zinc-800",
  "hover:text-zinc-900 dark:hover:text-zinc-100",
  // Typography
  {
    "font-medium": current,
  }
)}
```

**❌ Avoid - Array-based approach:**

```tsx
className={clsx(
  "base-styles",
  isCollapsed ? "collapsed-styles" : "expanded-styles",
  current && [
    "current-bg",
    "current-text",
    "current-font"
  ],
  isNavigating && "navigating-bg"
)}
```

### Benefits:

- **Organized by concern**: Layout, colors, backgrounds, etc.
- **Self-documenting**: Clear comments explain each group
- **Easier to maintain**: Find and modify related styles quickly
- **Better readability**: Consistent structure across components

