## Base UI Integration Guidelines

### Always Use `render=` Prop, Never `asChild`

When integrating with Base UI primitives, always use the `render=` prop pattern instead of `asChild`. The `asChild` prop is a Radix UI pattern that we don't use in this codebase.

**✅ Correct - Base UI `render=` prop:**

```tsx
// Base UI primitive renders the component
<BaseAlertDialog.Close
  render={<Button variant="destructive" />}
>
  Delete
</BaseAlertDialog.Close>

// Custom wrapper following the same pattern
<BaseDialog.Trigger
  render={<CustomButton {...props} />}
>
  Open Dialog
</BaseDialog.Trigger>
```

**❌ Incorrect - Radix `asChild` pattern:**

```tsx
// Don't use asChild - this is Radix UI pattern
<BaseAlertDialog.Close asChild>
  <Button variant="destructive">Delete</Button>
</BaseAlertDialog.Close>

// Also incorrect - component rendering primitive
<Button
  render={<BaseAlertDialog.Close />}
  variant="destructive"
>
  Delete
</Button>
```

### Benefits of `render=` Pattern:

- **Consistent with Base UI**: Follows Base UI's composition patterns
- **Better TypeScript**: Proper type inference and ref forwarding
- **Cleaner API**: Single component with render prop vs nested structure
- **Framework Agnostic**: Base UI's render pattern works across frameworks
